# ROS2_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md Sec 5.1/11 Phase 5. Requires state ERROR;
# ends in IDLE on success -- the only way back to IDLE from ERROR (Sec 6:
# ERROR otherwise has no recovery action). Mirrors BRIDGE_PROTOCOL.md
# Sec 5.11's already-designed (until now unimplemented) socket `reset`
# command, including its assume_gripper_empty flag: only the human knows
# whether a stick is still in the jaws after a failure, and that flag
# decides whether the "stick" collision object gets cleaned up here or
# left in place for subsequent planning to stay collision-aware around it.
# No feedback -- this is an instant state transition, not a multi-step
# sequence like the other three actions.

bool assume_gripper_empty
---
bool success
string message
---
